Role of metabolic conditions in cardiorenal diseases: Initiating pathways and therapeutic targeting. DASH, Dietary Approach to Stop Hypertension; HIIT, high-intensity interval training; NAD+, nicotinamide adenine nucleotide; NLRP3, nodular receptor protein 3; RAAS, renin–angiotensin–aldosterone system; RNS, reactive nitrogen species; ROS, reactive oxygen species; UA, uric acid.
A flowchart illustrating the mechanisms linking hyperglycemia, hyperuricemia, dyslipidemia, and obesity to chronic kidney disease (CKD) and cardiovascular disease (CVD). The upper section shows biological processes such as RAAS overactivation, mitochondrial dysfunction, insulin resistance, and chronic inflammation, contributing to CKD and CVD. The lower section presents therapeutic options, including lifestyle interventions (diets and exercise), pharmacological treatments (glucose-lowering drugs, statins), and novel targeted therapies (NAD+, taurine). Arrows indicate progression through the flowchart. Annotations and illustrations accompany each component.
